# =============================================================================
#  mustaphaukizuru.com · .gitignore
#  Node.js + Express + Prisma + React (Vite) full-stack monorepo.
# =============================================================================

# ── Secrets (NEVER commit) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
web/.env
web/.env.*
!web/.env.example

# ── B01 cleanup backups ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
backups/

# ── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# ── Build artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SPA bundle IS tracked. That is deliberate and it is load-bearing.
#
# The comment here used to say "scripts/deploy.sh rebuilds it on the server,
# so the generated files are not tracked". That was true of the manual
# deploy path and false of the one actually in use: production deploys via
# Hostinger Git auto-deploy (docs/PROJECT_DESCRIPTION.md), which clones
# master into a fresh hbuilds/versions/<uuid>/ and starts the app. It never
# runs deploy.sh and never builds the SPA.
#
# The result was a hard outage: the app booted, then every request 500d with
#   ENOENT: no such file or directory, stat ".../nodejs/public/index.html"
# because index.html was ignored here and therefore absent from the clone.
#
# So the bundle is committed. Rebuild with `npm run build` at the repo root
# and commit the result whenever web/src changes. Everything else under
# /public (images, fonts, cv, documents, flags, favicons, .htaccess, static
# error pages) is source and stays in git as before.
#
# Still ignored — regenerated per build and not needed to serve the app:
/public/__prerender/
# Runtime state raised by scripts/deploy.sh during the restart window.
/public/maintenance.flag
# Lighthouse CI reports — regenerated by every run, never source.
.lighthouseci/

dist/
build/
web/dist/
web/build/

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Runtime / caches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/
web/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
.eslintcache

# ── Prisma ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated Prisma Client lives inside node_modules; nothing to ignore here.
# But ignore any DB dumps or migration backups accidentally created locally.
*.sql.bak
prisma/migrations/.backup/

# ── Uploads (user-generated content, never in git) ──────────────────────────
uploads/
public/uploads/
public/media/
public/avatars/

# ── OS / Editor cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.history/

# ── Misc tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
# T4-4 · jest's JSON report, the source for the /about test count. Written by
# `npm run stats:build`, read once by generate-engineering-stats.mjs, and
# never committed — the NUMBERS are committed (public/engineering-stats.json),
# the 2 MB report they came from is not.
jest-results.json
.nyc_output/
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock
.env.local

# Workspace document folders (Cowork sessions)
mustaphaukizuru.com*Full-Stack SaaS Platform/

# Claude Code workspace — agent worktrees, session state, local settings.
# Previously committed by accident as a submodule gitlink, which broke
# `git submodule update --recursive` (used by GitHub Pages checkout).
# Never commit this directory.
.claude/


# Playwright (Q2)
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/

# Build-time sitemap fallback: regenerated by web/scripts/generate-sitemap.mjs.
# public/sitemap.xml must NOT exist — the web server would serve it instead of
# the dynamic, DB-backed /sitemap.xml route.
/public/sitemap.xml
/public/sitemap-static.xml
/web/public/sitemap-static.xml

# NOT ignored, and it must stay that way: public/og-static.json.
# It is generated the same way (web/scripts/generate-og-static.mjs, run by
# build:seo) but unlike the sitemap it is READ AT RUNTIME — the static-page
# branch of src/middleware/ogInjector.js loads it to answer crawlers. The
# sitemap file is only an offline fallback because a dynamic DB-backed route
# supersedes it; there is no such fallback here. Hostinger's Git deploy clones
# master and never builds (ADR 0001), so ignoring og-static.json would leave
# it absent in production and every static page would silently go back to the
# one generic English share card. Commit it with the build, like public/assets.

# Agent skill packs installed with `npx skills add` (.agents/skills/* plus the
# lockfile). Machine-local tooling, same class as .claude/ above: vendored
# third-party instruction files, megabytes of them, that no deploy needs and
# that would land inside the served tree. Reinstall with the commands in
# docs/AGENT_SKILLS.md rather than committing the contents.
/.agents/
/skills-lock.json
